BT 1 0 0 1 0 50 Tm /F1 10 Tf 12 TL .411147 Tw (Consider distributed tracing with OpenTelemetry. A span represents a unit of work and must often be linked) Tj T* 0 Tw .919223 Tw (to the currently-running span or request context. In Haskell today, that context is usually maintained either) Tj T* 0 Tw 1.464168 Tw (explicitly by threading arguments through the program or implicitly via ad-hoc thread-local state stored in) Tj T* 0 Tw 1.557397 Tw (library-managed maps. The former is tedious and error-prone; the latter is convenient, but it tends to be) Tj T* 0 Tw (awkward around concurrency, because child threads do not inherit the context.) Tj T* ET
